1
00:00:00,754 --> 00:00:03,051
Whilst you can build a single page

2
00:00:03,147 --> 00:00:06,183
application like this by using attributes

3
00:00:06,295 --> 00:00:06,665
like this,

4
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:10,037
there actually is an easier way of doing

5
00:00:10,150 --> 00:00:12,029
that if your goal is to

6
00:00:12,623 --> 00:00:15,851
give users that single page application like

7
00:00:15,931 --> 00:00:16,670
look and feel.

8
00:00:17,843 --> 00:00:21,039
Instead of setting that target and of using

9
00:00:21,296 --> 00:00:22,067
push URL,

10
00:00:22,677 --> 00:00:25,728
and instead of using hx-get here, you can go

11
00:00:25,793 --> 00:00:29,100
back to our regular anchor element as we had

12
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:31,396
it before without using HTMX here.

13
00:00:32,697 --> 00:00:35,025
And instead you can add a special attribute

14
00:00:35,106 --> 00:00:38,060
onto the body of your element or on any

15
00:00:38,237 --> 00:00:40,501
parent element of the element that should be

16
00:00:40,501 --> 00:00:43,038
controlled by HTMX. But here I wanna control

17
00:00:43,294 --> 00:00:45,591
all the elements on the page with HTMX

18
00:00:45,880 --> 00:00:48,689
because the attribute I'll add here on this

19
00:00:48,689 --> 00:00:51,660
body element is hx-boost.

20
00:00:52,630 --> 00:00:54,615
And that should be set to true here.

21
00:00:56,790 --> 00:00:59,243
Now, what does hx-boost do though?

22
00:00:59,969 --> 00:01:00,082
Well,

23
00:01:00,695 --> 00:01:03,149
this attribute boosts all

24
00:01:03,746 --> 00:01:07,074
anchor elements to be controlled by HTMX.

25
00:01:07,883 --> 00:01:10,618
And what that means is that now with

26
00:01:10,699 --> 00:01:12,253
hx-boost added here,

27
00:01:12,803 --> 00:01:12,851
all

28
00:01:13,385 --> 00:01:16,952
those anchor elements will actually send a

29
00:01:16,952 --> 00:01:19,420
GET request to their target URL

30
00:01:20,336 --> 00:01:23,453
and will swap the body of the current page

31
00:01:23,710 --> 00:01:26,506
for the body of the incoming response.

32
00:01:27,117 --> 00:01:29,736
So essentially, we'll get the behavior we

33
00:01:29,736 --> 00:01:30,331
had before

34
00:01:30,957 --> 00:01:34,059
but without manually adding hx-get and

35
00:01:34,251 --> 00:01:36,389
hx-target here and so on.

36
00:01:37,304 --> 00:01:40,084
We also don't need to manually update the

37
00:01:40,181 --> 00:01:42,591
URL because that will also be done by

38
00:01:42,671 --> 00:01:43,459
hx-boost.

39
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:48,140
So in the end, hx-boost is there to simplify

40
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:51,169
the process of building such a single page

41
00:01:51,169 --> 00:01:51,650
application.

42
00:01:53,029 --> 00:01:56,170
Because with it added here to this body on

43
00:01:56,234 --> 00:01:58,478
this page that renders all products,

44
00:01:59,520 --> 00:02:02,646
if I save that and reload, you see I get the

45
00:02:02,646 --> 00:02:04,041
same behavior as before.

46
00:02:04,794 --> 00:02:06,894
The URL is updated and I can use the back

47
00:02:06,974 --> 00:02:07,343
button

48
00:02:07,920 --> 00:02:10,324
and this refresh icon never changes to a

49
00:02:10,324 --> 00:02:10,612
cross.

50
00:02:11,302 --> 00:02:13,738
I got that same behavior, but now

51
00:02:14,331 --> 00:02:17,215
this works with help of hx-boost. And

52
00:02:17,231 --> 00:02:19,475
therefore, if you wanna build such a single

53
00:02:19,475 --> 00:02:20,485
page application

54
00:02:21,062 --> 00:02:23,001
where you technically never leave the

55
00:02:23,001 --> 00:02:25,437
current page, you can easily do that with

56
00:02:25,709 --> 00:02:28,498
hx-boost, which will convert all anchor

57
00:02:28,514 --> 00:02:31,864
elements to HTMX-controlled anchor elements.

58
00:02:32,681 --> 00:02:34,284
And it'll do even more than that.
